{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_IqylcZ8vXngmoAx0oO28IWi1","content":"1\t# Literature reading reference · plan r4\n2\t\n3\t**Status: r4, 2026-11-23. Approved under delegation (`auto=true`) in\n4\t[001-plan-gate.md](../001-plan-gate.md).** r4 applies the second and final\n5\tpanel round's five fixes, listed in §12, as amendments ruled at the gate.\n6\tr3 was the revision after the first panel round. r2 was the full plan `start-milestone` wrote from outline r1\n7\t(2026-11-22, merged in PR 229). The owner delegated `auto=true` for this\n8\tmilestone on 2026-11-23 and selected the full GND panel for plan and close\n9\treview (D6). The first round read r2\n10\t([r2 panel](../../../reviews/literature-reading-reference-r2-panel/README.md));\n11\tr3 applies its seven fixes, listed in §11. Approval is recorded only in a\n12\tplan-gate record, which does not exist yet.\n13\t\n14\tThis plan covers one open issue,\n15\t[#226](https://github.com/vasiloglou/gnd-public/issues/226): a host reading\n16\tscientific papers with GND's literature stages measured about 30 % recall for\n17\tevery model it tried and has no reference point to tell its own loss from the\n18\tmethod's.\n19\t\n20\t**Provenance.** Phase IDs LR1–LR3 and decisions D1–D5 are the outline's. r2\n21\tadds criteria IDs, obligations H1–H22 and decisions D6–D9. The outline left\n22\ttwo rows \"not read\". Both are read now, and both change the plan `(r2)`:\n23\t\n24\t- **LR1.** `gnd verify --format json` already lists every failing constraint\n25\t  with its rows (H2). What is missing is a page that says so, the rows in the\n26\t  text output, and the constraint's declared id (H3, H4).\n27\t- **LR2.** The reading example has no quote and refuses none (H8). The 44\n28\t  claims #226 lost to \"quote outside the shown section\" were dropped by the\n29\t  reporter's own host. GND's one binding of a quote to text is the anchor\n30\t  check, against the whole document a sidecar names (H10).\n31\t\n32\tr3 adds H23–H25 and re-ran H2–H4 and H22 at `11a7ebf7` `(r3)`. Code\n33\tcitations were read at `548b9a1d` (`main`, 2026-11-23). `main` moved to\n34\t`78934ee3` the same day (PR 234, PR 236, PR 237) while this plan was written;\n35\tthose merges changed planning files and six skill scripts that dev-tools\n36\tdelivers, and nothing under `src`, `tests` or `docs`. H17 and §3 are brought\n37\tup to them `(m)`. Rows marked\n38\t\"agent\" were read by the read-only harvest agent of this session and not all\n39\tre-read by the author; the rows the plan rests on (H2, H3, H4, H8, H9, H10,\n40\tH13) were re-read or run by the author.\n41\t\n42\t## Goal and completion predicates\n43\t\n44\tA host that reads papers with GND's literature stages can tell whether a low\n45\trecall is its own loss or the method's, can see why a source fails\n46\tverification, and knows where a quote may come from.\n47\t\n48\t- **LR1.** For a source that `gnd verify` fails, a host lists the constraints\n49\t  that failed and the rows that violate each, from one documented place. A\n50\t  test holds the documented steps on a packaged failing source.\n51\t- **LR2.** The pages state one rule for where a quoted span may lie: inside\n52\t  the document the anchor sidecar names, by digest. They say what that means\n53\t  for a host that shows the model one section at a time, and a test holds\n54\t  both sides of the rule.\n55\t- **LR3.** A labelled set ships with the literature example. A recorded run\n56\t  of the reading stages over it reports recall and precision per stage\n57\t  setting, names the producer and settings, and replays with zero producer\n58\t  calls.\n59\t\n60\tThe milestone is closed when each phase has its record and the close record\n61\tcites green focused gates for LR1–LR3, the structure and inventory guards,\n62\t`uv run ruff check` `(r3)`, the component-index check, a drafted\n63\treply to #226, and a close review on the instrument D6 selects.\n64\t\n65\t## 0. Binding design rules\n66\t\n67\t- **R0.1 Formats stay.** The anchor sidecar and the default `gnd verify`\n68\t  payload and text keep their fields and bytes; #226 says they work as they\n69\t  are. Anything LR1 adds is opt-in or a page (D7).\n70\t- **R0.2 A reference figure is a measurement of one run.** It names the\n71\t  producer, the settings and the labelled set. It is not a claim about other\n72\t  corpora or models, and the page says so beside every figure.\n73\t- **R0.3 No fidelity rate in the `verify` payload.** `gnd verify` keeps\n74\t  saying that checker acceptance is not proof of faithfulness\n75\t  (`src/gnd/skills/gnd-extract/references/extraction-contract.md:152`); the reference figures live in the\n76\t  example's own record.\n77\t- **R0.4 Fixture bytes stay.** The packaged reading run, its pinned producer\n78\t  table and its recorded outputs are byte-identical after LR1 and LR2. LR3\n79\t  adds a second fixture beside them and changes none.\n80\t- **R0.5 The gate calls no model.** A live run happens once, under the\n81\t  owner's explicit selection of a producer and a budget (D3). Every gate\n82\t  replays recorded responses.\n83\t- **R0.6 One home per rule.** How to read a failed verification has one\n84\t  home (D8); the quote rule lives in `docs/reference/anchors.md`; the\n85\t  literature pages cite both.\n86\t\n87\tThe project's six standing rules\n88\t(`.codex/skills/process-phase/references/project.md`) and the rule \"General\n89\tsolutions, not pattern-matched ones\" (`AGENTS.md`) bind every phase; each\n90\tspec discharges them by name.\n91\t\n92\t## 1. Scope, sources and authority\n93\t\n94\tHarvested obligations. \"Observed\" means read or run by the author at\n95\t`548b9a1d` on 2026-11-23; \"agent\" means read by the harvest agent;\n96\t\"inherited\" means claimed by a source and not re-measured.\n97\t\n98\t| # | Source | Obligation | Kind | Phase |\n99\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n100\t| H1 | #226 request 3 | \"A way to see why `verify` reports `alethic-failure` per source: which constraint, on which rows.\" The reporter saw it on all 20 sources (3,729 rows, 280 of them unanchored) | inherited | LR1 |\n101\t| H2 | probe `(r3)`: run `python -m gnd.examples.literature.reading run --out RUN`, copy `reading_fixture/reading.orm.json` and its include `depth_fixture/vocabulary.orm.json` into `RUN`, then `gnd verify RUN/reading.orm.json RUN/reported-conflict.population.json --no-extraction --format json`. The include resolves beside the model file, so the vocabulary must sit there; `reading_fixture/` alone does not hold it | exit 1, `outcome: \"violated\"`, `schema_version: 7`, `counts.fail: 1`. The one failing verdict carries `constraint_ref` (`fact_types[subject_label].constraints[0]`), `constraint_type` (`uniqueness`), `modality` (`alethic`), `source`, `status`, a `message` that verbalizes the constraint with the violating value, and `offending_facts`, the two violating rows in full. Each verdict also carries `verdict` (`fail`) and `reason_code`; the report itself carries `outcome` and `counts` `(r3)` | observed (re-run at `11a7ebf7`) | LR1 |\n102\t| H3 | the same probe, text output | one line under `BLOCKING (alethic)`: `[fail] <constraint_ref>: <message>`. The rows are not printed; the value appears only inside the message | observed | LR1 |\n103\t| H4 | the same probe; `commands/checking.py:904` | the constraint's declared id (`subject_has_one_label`) is not in the payload. `gnd verify --rule-ids` is refused (\"unrecognized arguments\"); the flag exists on `gnd check` only | observed | LR1 (D7) |\n104\t| H5 | `redaction.py:616-633` | when a model's redaction policy selects a verdict's roles, `message` becomes a fixed marker and `offending_facts` one marker row. A host of such a model sees which constraint failed and not the rows | observed by reading | LR1 |\n105\t| H6 | `docs/guides/documents.md:62-72`; `src/gnd/skills/gnd-extract/references/extraction-contract.md:136-148` | the pages say \"Read the `extraction` block and the semantic verdicts independently\" and \"REPORT IT\" for exit 1. No page shows how to list the failing constraints and their rows from a verify report. `offending_facts` is shown on the expense and book tutorial pages, for the Python `check` call, and on no verify page | observed | LR1 |\n106\t| H7 | #226 request 2; \"What we measured\" | 82 claims dropped host-side: 44 quoted text outside the shown section, 38 used a participant or predicate not in the quote. \"Nearly half of our drops were quotes from elsewhere in the paper, and many looked correct\" | inherited | LR2 |\n107\t| H8 | `src/gnd/examples/literature/reading.py:176-193` | a producer response is `{outcome, facts, proposal_keys}`. There is no quote in it and no check of one. Each attempt records the shown section's span and `excerpt_sha256`, which binds the attempt to the section, not a claim to a quote | observed | LR2 |\n108\t| H9 | `src/gnd/examples/literature/reading.py:258-286`, `:390-395` | the example verifies two kinds of document. For the broad and targeted passes it is the attempted sections of one pass joined with newlines, not the declared source and not one shown section; for the reported conflict it is `conflict.txt` `(r4)`. Each verify writes an extraction sidecar that binds its document by digest, and no anchor sidecar, so the example is not a model for anchoring `(r3, r4)` | observed | LR2 |\n109\t| H10 | `anchors.py:238-271`; `docs/reference/anchors.md:41-45` | `bind_anchors` requires the sidecar's `document_sha256` to equal the digest of the document bytes, and each anchor's span to lie inside that document with a matching `excerpt_sha256`; otherwise `anchor:binding-mismatch`. `block_id` and `unit_id` are free labels. So a quote is bound to a document version, never to a section | observed | LR2 |\n110\t| H11 | `src/gnd/examples/literature/reading.py:93-112` | a roster section is `source`, `kind`, `span` (byte offsets, increasing per source) and `selection` (`opening` or `targeted`); an unavailable section has no span and a reason | observed | LR2, LR3 |\n111\t| H12 | #226 request 1 | \"A reference recall (and precision) for the literature-reading stages on a labelled set, with the stage settings that produced it\" | inherited | LR3 |\n112\t| H13 | `src/gnd/examples/literature/reading.py:42`, `:311-341`; `docs/literature/index.md:309-313` | the example's only recall figure is fidelity recall over two fact types (`CALIBRATION_FACTS`), 2 of 2 and 1 of 2, used to qualify one scoped absence. No precision is measured | observed | LR3 |\n113\t| H14 | #226 \"What we measured\" | on 20 papers and about 100 gold claims: broad pass best recall 29 of 101 with precision 15 to 38 %; targeted pass best recall 30 of 100 with precision 10 to 20 %; 233 kept claims outside the gold passages; 3 of 29 aligned claims agree on the predicate | inherited | LR3 (comparison rows) |\n114\t| H15 | `src/gnd/examples/literature/reading.py:149-158`, `:562-584` | the producer is duck-typed (`produce(stage, section)`); `run()` wires the saved producer; `replay()` re-derives from the retained table with zero producer calls and requires byte identity, for the packaged fixture only | observed | LR3 |\n115\t| H16 | `src/gnd/examples/literature/reading.py:587-596` | a run's settings are `--budget-bytes` and `--scenario`; broad against targeted is fixed per section in the roster. There is no other stage setting to report | observed | LR3 (D9) |\n116\t| H17 | [literature-host-interfaces](../../literature-host-interfaces/README.md) plan r6, approved by the owner on 2026-11-23 (PR 237) `(m)` | LH1: a public producer protocol in the reading example, a caller's producer driving the six stages over a caller's root. LH2: `replay()` of a live run from its own folder with zero producer calls, its settings read from the run. LH1 has a draft spec waiting for its owner gate; nothing is implemented | observed by reading | LR3 needs both |\n117\t| H18 | literature-depth close, `016-milestone-close.md:162` | \"Hos