bserved | LR3 (D1, D4) |\n124\t| H25 `(r3)` | `tests/test_packaged_skills.py:101-125` | a relative link from a packaged skill file must resolve inside the packaged skills tree, so a skill page cites a `docs/` page by absolute URL | observed by reading | LR1 (D8) |\n125\t\n126\tComponent index (`dev/components/`), searched 2026-11-23:\n127\t\n128\t| Capability | Search | Found |\n129\t|---|---|---|\n130\t| verify a population | `search \"verify population\"` | `cli.verify_command`, `export.verification` |\n131\t| the reading example | `search \"literature reading\"` | `examples.literature_reading` (`reading.py`), `examples.literature_assurance` |\n132\t| bind a quote to text | `search \"anchor quote\"` | no component of its own; `src/gnd/anchors.py` is found by `git grep bind_anchors` |\n133\t| score a reading against labels | `search \"literature reading\"` | `assurance_report.py`: `score_reading_coverage` scores coverage; `_semantic` and `_source_binding` score precision and recall against the regression corpus's answer key (H24). r2's \"scores coverage, not recall against gold\" was wrong `(r3)` |\n134\t\n135\t`components_index.py review` lists 276 leads in 10 groups; an index review\n136\tis offered to the owner and is not a prerequisite.\n137\t\n138\t### Issue requests and the phases that discharge them\n139\t\n140\t| Request | Phase |\n141\t|---|---|\n142\t| #226: a way to see why `verify` fails a source, by constraint and row | LR1 |\n143\t| #226: guidance on whether a claim's quote must lie inside the shown section | LR2 |\n144\t| #226: a reference recall and precision on a labelled set, with the settings | LR3 |\n145\t\n146\tThis is a framework milestone. An experiment-claim census (`gnd coverage`)\n147\tcounts claims over a domain model; it does not measure a reader's recall or\n148\tsay what a report page explains, so none is read here. The baseline is rows\n149\tH2, H3, H13 and H14.\n150\t\n151\t## 2. Contract proposal and product behavior\n152\t\n153\t##