67\t  citing line, an absolute URL to the docs home (H25) `(r3)`; its manifest is held by `tests/test_packaged_skills.py`, in\n268\t  the guard block.\n269\t- **Release notes.** One entry per phase under the unreleased heading.\n270\t- **Compatibility.** LR1 and LR2 change pages and tests only, under D7 (a)\n271\t  and D2 (b). D7 (c) would add an opt-in flag and keeps the default bytes.\n272\t  D7 (b) as written changes the default text, so ruling it would amend R0.1\n273\t  and LR1-C5 at the same gate `(r3)`. r2 said \"the default bytes stay either\n274\t  way\", which was wrong for (b). LR3 adds a\n275\t  fixture and changes none.\n276\t- **Issue reply.** `(r4)` An interim draft covering requests 3 and 2 is\n277\t  written in LR2 and updated when LR2 merges; the close writes the final\n278\t  draft with LR3's figures. The owner posts both.\n279\t\n280\t## 6. Risks and required controls\n281\t\n282\t| Risk | Control |\n283\t|---|---|\n284\t| The page describes fields the report does not carry, or stops matching it | LR1-C3: the test reads the page's field names and checks each against the schema and a live report |\n285\t| The documented steps are fitted to one fixture | LR1-C1, C2 and C4 cover a failure, a pass, a deontic warning and a redacted verdict; the diff review's pattern-matched claim |\n286\t| A host reads \"anywhere in the document\" as \"any text is evidence\" | LR2 states the two things an anchor does prove (the span is in that document version and the excerpt matches) and that neither proves the claim is supported |\n287\t| A reference figure is read as a product claim | R0.2, with the set, producer and settings beside every figure (LR3-C5) |\n288\t| The labelled set carries text that cannot be redistributed | D1 (a), with the licence of each source recorded in the set (LR3-C1) |\n289\t| A live run needs a provider credential | R0.5: made once under the owner's explicit selection; the gate replays it. No repository `.env` is read |\n290\t| The scoring