362\t| D5 | Whether LR1 and LR2 ship ahead of LR3, by their own pull request | Yes `(r2)`. They need no other milestone, and LR3 waits for literature-host-interfaces. The outline proposed holding them so the three replies go out together; LR3 now waits for two phases of another milestone. `(r3)` An interim reply to #226 covering requests 3 and 2 is drafted when LR2 merges (`notes/issue-reply.md`); the owner posts it. If LH1 or LH2 is not on `main` when LR1 and LR2 close, LR3 waits and the milestone stays open; carrying LR3 is the owner's decision |\n363\t| D6 | Plan review and close review instrument | **Ruled by the owner, 2026-11-23: \"Full panel, both\"** `(o)`. The full GND panel for plan and close review. r2's proposal, superseded: \"the GND panel light for both\" |\n364\t| D7 `(r2)` | LR1: does `gnd verify` change. (a) No: the JSON report already answers the request and the phase is a page and a test. (b) (a), and the text output prints each failing verdict's rows under its line. (c) (a), and `gnd verify` accepts `--rule-ids` as `gnd check` does, so a verdict carries the constraint's declared id | (a). #226 asks for no format change (H19). (c) is the one that would let a host name a constraint by its id and not by position; it is offered, not proposed |\n365\t| D8 `(r2)` | LR1: the one home of \"Reading a failed verification\". (a) `docs/guides/documents.md`, after the verify command. (b) `extraction-contract.md` §5, in the packaged skill. (c) `docs/reference/cli.md` | (a); the other two cite it |\n366\t| D9 `(r2)` | LR3: what \"stage settings\" means, given that a run has only a budget and a scenario (H16) | The record names the producer, the budget and the roster's split into opening and targeted sections, read from the settings LH2 writes into a run, and the prompt of each stage if LH2 records it. If LH2 does not, LR3's spec either records the prompts in LR3's own record or asks for a `reading.py` settings field after LH2 merges, one writer at a time (§3) `