\tit); Kimi's claim that an include resolves against the working directory (a\n396\trun from the parent folder exits 1; what is true, that the vocabulary must be\n397\tstaged beside the model, is in H2). Codex's note that `project.md` says\n398\t\"There is no component index in this repository\" is a stale line in\n399\t`project.md` itself, which its later \"Component index\" section, `AGENTS.md`\n400\tand the sibling plans contradict; the check stays, and the stale line is\n401\treported as a follow-up, not edited here.\n402\t\n403\t## 12. r4: the second panel round's fixes\n404\t\n405\tThe second and final round\n406\t([r3 panel](../../../reviews/literature-reading-reference-r3-panel/README.md))\n407\tread r3 at SHA-256\n408\t`a1ab8a9c87e7b733eea0b42a5306173385e4c9c44319b96767af82ac0172a299`. Three of\n409\tsix seats succeeded (quorum); none raised a blocking concern. Under the stop\n410\trule of §8 there is no third round: the five fixes are applied here and\n411\truled at the plan gate.\n412\t\n413\t| Fix | What r4 changes | Sites |\n414\t|---|---|---|\n415\t| fix-interim-reply | the interim reply is an LR2 deliverable; §5 names both drafts | §3 LR2 row, §5 |\n416\t| fix-example-verify-paths | both verify paths; \"no anchor sidecar\" | H9, §2 LR2, LR2-C5 |\n417\t| fix-corpus-reuse-only | D1 (d) reuses the corpus with an overlay and changes none of its bytes; the LR3 lane names its tests | §2 LR3, D1, §9 |\n418\t| fix-lr1-disclosure-and-levels | LR1 cites the disclosure home; the redacting fixture edits the vocabulary; `GND_DISCLOSURE` pinned; three-level field check | §2 LR1, §3 Fixtures, LR1-C3 |\n419\t| fix-plan-gate-wording | the gate rules under delegation; full skill path | §8, R0.3, H6 |\n420\t\n421\t## 13. Close amendments\n422\t\n423\tMade at milestone close on 2026-11-23 under the `auto=true` delegation, from\n424\tthe refuted premises and open rows of the phase records. Each keeps the\n425\tprior wording.\n426\t\n427\t| # | Raised in | Prior wording | 